{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/988123-peach-gleaming-horizon-flash-a-glorious-solar-saber-evocation","id":988123,"title":"[PEACH] Gleaming Horizon Flash - A Glorious Solar Saber Evocation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T21:44:31-07:00","id":988123,"title":"[PEACH] Gleaming Horizon Flash - A Glorious Solar Saber Evocation","content":"Hi guys! I'm in a 3E campaign, and I've recently picked up Glorious Solar Saber. Now, I'm also a huge Warframe fan, and I got to thinking: 'man, GSS is basically perfect for modelling Excalibur's awesome Exalted (hah) Blade ability. So I've come up with an Evocation to pul off another of his more iconic abilities: the Radial Blind.<br /> <br /> I used Blinding Fang Strike as a conceptual basis, but scaled it up and amped up the cost a bit in order to account for its AoE nature. I tied its range to anima expenditure, too, because it seemed thematic to do so. I'm looking for critiques to balance it, though. Thus:<br /> <br /> Gleaming Horizon Flash<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp, 1+a; Mins: --<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Prerequisite Charms: --<br /> <br /> Channeling his anima through the radiant shaft of his Solar Saber, the Lawgiver unleashes a wave of blinding energies. This evocation may not be used while the Solar's anima is at its dim level or below. Upon use, the Solar's anima regresses to its dim level. At the Glowing level, this evocation reaches only those who are within Close range, however for each level beyond Glowing, Gleaming Horizon Flash's range increases by one interval, to a maximum of Medium at Bonfire level.<br /> <br /> The Solar makes a special combat gambit difficulty of 3. On a success, all targets within range suffer a -3 penalty to all actions that persists for [1 + Essence] rounds, after which the penalty diminishes at a rate of 1 per round. Creatures that do not possess eyes or the capability for sight are unaffected by Gleaming Horizon Flash, unless they are creatures of darkness such as demons, ghosts or their associates.<br /> <br /> This evocation also illuminates the affected region as if it were midday, lasting until the effects of the evocation fade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12557-stormgear","name":"Stormgear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:28:12-07:00","id":988137,"title":"","content":"The idea is solid and I like it very much. I'd just like to give you a couple of pointers:<br /> <br /> - You did not include an essence prerequisite for the evocation.<br /> - Anima levels as a cost for charms is codified by the book in the format Xa (even if some sections of it don't stick to it as they should) so you should use that notation instead of cluttering the charm text.<br /> - The interaction between anima levels and range is confusingly worded; compare it with Blazing Solar Bolt (pg 353) which has a similar effect.<br /> - The penalties you describe are essentially blindness penalties, which are already defined by the book. Use those instead.<br /> - This takes a turn to use and the penalties aren't very heavy, so I'd suggest dropping the gambit and having it succeed automatically (this also requires fewer rolls, which is generally good). If you want to keep aspects of the gambit, give it an initiative cost and make it perilous. If you do that then you should also drop the willpower cost.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:00:30-07:00","id":988143,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe something like this?<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> Gleaming Horizon Flash<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp, 1+a; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: --<br /> Prerequisite Charms: --<br /> <br /> Channeling his anima through the radiant shaft of his Solar Saber, the Lawgiver unleashes a wave of blinding energies. This evocation may not be used while the Solar's anima below the glowing level. Upon use, the Solar's anima regresses to its dim level. Gleaming Horizon Flash affects all targets within close range. In addition, the Charm\u2019s range can be increased by spending anima levels at a rate of one level per increase, allowing the Solar to strike opponents up to medium range.<br /> <br /> All targets within range suffer a -3 penalty to all actions that persists for [1 + Essence] rounds, after which the penalty diminishes at a rate of 1 per round. Creatures that do not possess eyes or the capability for sight are unaffected by Gleaming Horizon Flash, unless they are creatures of darkness such as demons, ghosts or their associates.<br /> <br /> This evocation also illuminates the affected region as if it were midday, lasting until the effects of the evocation fade.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> How's that look? Thanks a lot for the help, by the way! I kept the 1+a notation for the anima expenditure due to that better representing the actual costs of the evocation. Also, I kept the text on the charm's specific effects just for my own bookkeeping. It'd be a pain to keep flipping back to page 168 every time, after all. I also tried to clear up the language on the range, too. Looked at Blazing Solar Bolt and used it as reference. Also dropped the decisive-only tag because it's no longer a gambit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12557-stormgear","user":"Stormgear","date":". 10-16-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12557-stormgear","name":"Stormgear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T03:04:50-07:00","id":988195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stormgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/988123-peach-gleaming-horizon-flash-a-glorious-solar-saber-evocation?p=988143#post988143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, maybe something like this?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit powerful and your still lacking the essence requirement for unlocking this evocation. (which is very important in determining if its too powerful or not for its gating level)<br /> <br /> Having the blindness effect last 1 + essence rounds is fine at low essence levels, but at essence 3-5 the penalty lasts as long as many regular combats lasts. And this is not taking into effect the two rounds which it is still in effect just at reduced penalty level. <br /> <br /> 1+ essence/2 rounded up is probably more balanced. This is probably still in the high essence range. 4-5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T08:59:08-07:00","id":988266,"title":"","content":"Updated the essence mins. Also note that Gleaming Horizon Flash doesn't actually have IFF. It'll hit everything, friend and foe alike. I'm pretty sure that might balance it more.<br /> <br /> Maybe I can just cap the duration to 3 rounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12557-stormgear","name":"Stormgear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:36:46-07:00","id":988282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stormgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/988123-peach-gleaming-horizon-flash-a-glorious-solar-saber-evocation?p=988266#post988266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated the essence mins. Also note that Gleaming Horizon Flash doesn't actually have IFF. It'll hit everything, friend and foe alike. I'm pretty sure that might balance it more.<br /> <br /> Maybe I can just cap the duration to 3 rounds?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 3 rounds cap is probably a good adjustment, id still bump the essence requirement to 3 or 4. Its a great effect, as your still affected by it for 5 rounds with the current cap. Id contemplate cutting it to 2 full rounds of blindness before it starts to reduce the penalty. You should test it out. Its often hard to get the balancing correctly without play testing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:34:11-07:00","id":988366,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's go third draft! I think at this point I might have to actually play with it in-game to see whether it's too crazy or not.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Gleaming Horizon Flash<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp, 1+a; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: --<br /> Prerequisite Charms: -- (Glorious Solar Saber)<br /> <br /> Channeling his anima through the radiant shaft of his Solar Saber, the Lawgiver unleashes a wave of blinding energies. This evocation may not be used while the Solar's anima below the glowing level. Upon use, the Solar's anima regresses to its dim level. Gleaming Horizon Flash affects all targets within close range. In addition, the Charm\u2019s range can be increased by spending anima levels at a rate of one level per increase, allowing the Solar to strike opponents up to medium range.<br /> <br /> All targets within range suffer a -3 penalty to all actions that persists for [1 + Essence/2] rounds, after which the penalty diminishes at a rate of 1 per round. Creatures that do not possess eyes or the capability for sight are unaffected by Gleaming Horizon Flash, unless they are creatures of darkness such as demons, ghosts or their associates.<br /> <br /> This evocation also illuminates the affected region as if it were midday, lasting until the effects of the evocation fade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12557-stormgear","name":"Stormgear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}